hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15793","Hashim narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from a freedman of Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah al-Adawi, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in our house while I was a boy. He said: I went to go out to play, and my mother said: O Abd Allah, come, I will give you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What did you intend to give him? She said: I will give him dates. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you, had you not done so, a lie would have been written against you."
